course: dictionary
lesson: 2349
title: New words for new things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new because the world has new things in it. A cryptocurrency is a kind of money that lives on computers, not in your pocket. You can work out its meaning from the words around it, which are its context.
explain: The dictionary says a cryptocurrency uses special codes to keep it secure, and that no government or bank issues it. The sentence «Bitcoin is the most famous cryptocurrency» tells you that Bitcoin is one example of this kind of money.
explain: The sentence «its price has been reported to jump up and down a lot» is another clue. Prices that jump up and down show that the value changes quickly. To check, swap in your meaning: "Bitcoin is the most famous digital money that uses special codes" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
fact: A cryptocurrency is a kind of digital money that exists only on computers.
fact: It uses special codes to keep it secure.
fact: It is not issued by a government or a bank.
fact: Bitcoin is an example of a cryptocurrency, and «crypto» is the informal short name for it.
fact: The price can jump up and down very fast, for example from £20,000 to £50,000, which is up £30,000.
exercise: «Bitcoin is the most famous cryptocurrency.» What is a cryptocurrency? | A card you use to pay for sweets | A shop that sells computers | A coin you find in a pirate's chest | *A kind of digital money that exists only on computers
exercise: In the example, the price went from £20,000 to £50,000. How much did it go up? | £20,000 | £70,000 | £10,000 | *£30,000
exercise: Which word is the informal, short name for cryptocurrency? | digital | bitcoin | *crypto | currency
test: What do the special codes in a cryptocurrency do? | *To keep it secure | To make it heavier | To change its colour | To stop people reading the news
test: Is a cryptocurrency issued by a government or a bank? | Yes, but only banks do it | Yes, always | *No, it is not | Yes, but only the government does it
exam: Which sentence shows that cryptocurrency prices change quickly? | «Bitcoin is the most famous cryptocurrency.» | «Cryptocurrency is explained in money lessons.» | «Crypto is the informal short name.» | *«Its price has been reported to jump up and down a lot.»
